(6092646, 892689, 29011, '<td valign="top">I''m with Deb. The colors are pop out of the screen. Nice detail to boot as well.</td>', 'I''m with Deb. The colors are pop out of the screen. Nice detail to boot as well.', '2010-07-14 12:45:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6098110, 892571, 43463, '<td valign="top">And good for vitamin C too;-) The red of the tomato really stands out from the white of the refrigerator. I really like the idea in the composition and the wry humor. I think that the whites could pop a little more - be more of a crisp white; getting rid or cutting down the shadows on this would help. Yeah, I am a nut to suggest bring lights to the fridge to light up the inner workings, but I really think it would make the whites whiter (maybe high key a bit) such that the red tomato really, really, stands out. The other thing that would improve the composition is that the there is some odd noise very visible in the bottom right corner. Some faint yellowish green artifact noise is what I see on the monitor (don''t know if you can see it for all monitors are not created equal which is a real pain)</td>', 'And good for vitamin C too;-) The red of the tomato really stands out from the white of the refrigerator. I really like the idea in the composition and the wry humor. I think that the whites could pop a little more - be more of a crisp white; getting rid or cutting down the shadows on this would help. Yeah, I am a nut to suggest bring lights to the fridge to light up the inner workings, but I really think it would make the whites whiter (maybe high key a bit) such that the red tomato really, really, stands out. The other thing that would improve the composition is that the there is some odd noise very visible in the bottom right corner. Some faint yellowish green artifact noise is what I see on the monitor (don''t know if you can see it for all monitors are not created equal which is a real pain)', '2010-07-20 12:08:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6098117, 892321, 43463, '<td valign="top">Lovely colors! There really is the explosion of vivid purples and yellows in this composition. It makes me think of an exploding floral star. Composition is strong and colors really pop. One thing that would improve the appeal of the image is to get the center portion of the flower in sharper focus. It is juusst I touch soft. All points of the flower could be in sharper crisp focus if you increase the F-stop to something higher than 5.6 (for greater depth of field). A macro of an object can be very tricky if you have some points of the flower higher or lower than where you are focusing. Hence some softness to some of the elments. With adjusting the aperature to get greater DOF you will have to adjust the shutter to a slower speed to expose it correctly.</td>', 'Lovely colors! There really is the explosion of vivid purples and yellows in this composition. It makes me think of an exploding floral star. Composition is strong and colors really pop. One thing that would improve the appeal of the image is to get the center portion of the flower in sharper focus. It is juusst I touch soft. All points of the flower could be in sharper crisp focus if you increase the F-stop to something higher than 5.6 (for greater depth of field). A macro of an object can be very tricky if you have some points of the flower higher or lower than where you are focusing. Hence some softness to some of the elments. With adjusting the aperature to get greater DOF you will have to adjust the shutter to a slower speed to expose it correctly.', '2010-07-20 12:15:51.000000', NULL, 0),
